  "honest_note": "R7 and R8 run as parallel hop-0 sources (hot/cold precedent). The textbook R7->Dm8 chromatic pathway is PRESENT in the real rows (Dm8 tw=38836, Dm8a/Dm8b/Dm9 also land). R8's named rows split into subtype rows (yellow/pale/dorsal-margin); only the main-class aggregate row is used per downstream class \u2014 subtype rows are not summed (would double-count). The 49542/49540 duplicated tier is represented by its most specific member (49542). Dm8's own downstream failed ALL query forms (grouped x2, named x1) \u2014 honest hop-1 terminal, not faked. Hop-2 nodes that dilute below the toy cascade's 0.15 threshold are real edges with toy-quiet readouts.\n\nHOP-2 RETRY 2026-10-15 (API recovered): retried the 8 hop-1 nodes that had no hop-2 edges. Landed: FBbt_00053385 (1 new hop-2 nodes). Still terminal (all query forms failed or no specific downstream): FBbt_00059247, FBbt_00047096, FBbt_00005127, FBbt_00003767, FBbt_00013774, FBbt_00053639, FBbt_00110136. Dm8's own downstream was retried with the full fallback chain.",
  "behavior": {
    "text": "Color vision: R7/R8 chromatic photoreceptors drive medulla interneurons \u2014 including the Dm8 amacrine family that computes chromatic opponency \u2014 fanning into columnar and intrinsic visual pathways toward the central brain.",
    "basis": "R7/R8 as the chromatic photoreceptors and Dm8 as their color-opponency target is textbook Drosophila (Heath et al; Dm8 pools R7 input for UV-vs-visible comparisons). All edges here are measured FlyWire synapse counts."
